+# Security Audit – The Daily Grind (static site)
+
+## Findings
+
+| # | Area | Finding | Severity | Status |
+|---|------|---------|----------|--------|
+| 1 | Headers | No Content-Security-Policy was set. | High | Fixed: `<meta>` CSP plus header CSP |
+| 2 | Headers | No clickjacking protection (`frame-ancestors` / `X-Frame-Options`). | Medium | Fixed: headers, plus a JS frame-buster fallback |
+| 3 | Headers | No HSTS, `nosniff`, Referrer-Policy, Permissions-Policy or COOP. | Medium | Fixed in `_headers` / `vercel.json` |
+| 4 | Markup | Inline `<style>` block and `style=""` attribute forced `style-src 'unsafe-inline'`. | Low | Fixed: moved to `styles.css` |
+| 5 | Markup | Third-party image (images.unsplash.com) loaded from CSS. | Info | Allowed explicitly in `img-src` |
+| 6 | Markup | `/logout` is a plain GET link, so a third-party page could log users out (CSRF). | Low | Needs a backend change: make logout a POST with a CSRF token. Not changed here because the server routes aren't in this repo. |
+| 7 | Scripts | The page had no client-side scripts, so there were no DOM XSS sinks. | Info | Trusted Types enforced so it stays that way |
+
+## Policies
+
+- **CSP**: `default-src 'none'`, with only same-origin scripts and styles,
+  Unsplash images, `base-uri 'none'`, `object-src 'none'`,
+  `form-action 'self'`, `frame-ancestors 'none'`, Trusted Types
+  (`require-trusted-types-for 'script'; trusted-types 'none'`) and
+  `upgrade-insecure-requests`.
+- **Delivery**: `index.html` has a `<meta>` CSP, so the policy also applies on
+  the static dev server, which can't send headers. `_headers` (Netlify /
+  Cloudflare) and `vercel.json` send the full set of headers.
+- **Safe rollout**: the same policy is also sent as
+  `Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only` with `report-to` / `report-uri`
+  `/csp-reports`. Change new policies in Report-Only first, check the
+  violation reports, then promote them to the enforcing header. If you add a
+  script that needs DOM sinks, define a named Trusted Types policy and list it
+  in `trusted-types`.
+- **HSTS** is sent without `preload`. Add `preload` only after you've
+  confirmed that every subdomain serves HTTPS.
+
+## Rules for future changes
+
+- Don't use inline `<script>`, `on*=` handlers or `style=""` attributes. Put
+  the code in external files under `'self'`.
+- Any new third-party origin must be added to the CSP on purpose, in all
+  three places.
+- Third-party scripts must use `integrity` (SRI) and `crossorigin`.
+- Links with `target="_blank"` must have `rel="noopener noreferrer"`.
